P9 (issue #23, U19): no 16-items machine for the unrecoded surrogates of
the shuffle method.

For -gs the data are not recoded (FPG_NORECODE|FPG_NOSORT keep the table
columns), so item codes do not follow the item frequencies and
infrequent items stay in the transactions, but fpg_data(FPG_SURR) still
packs the items with codes below 16 for the simple and single variants
(-As, -Ad with -l > 0), and the miners then lose or miscount item sets
(fpgrowth-core.md B8): wrong spectra, e.g. a non-integer average number
of single items, which a column shuffle keeps exactly. Clearing the
FPG_FIM16 field of the mode for -gs disables the machine in every
miner; it is an optimization only.

--- a/fpgrowth/src/fpgpsp.c
+++ b/fpgrowth/src/fpgpsp.c
@@ -266,6 +266,8 @@
   assert(tabag                  /* check the function arguments */
   &&    (algo >= FPG_SIMPLE) && (algo <= FPG_TOPDOWN));
   if (seed == 0) seed = (long)time(NULL);
+  if (surr == FPG_SHUFFLE)      /* P9: no 16-items machine for */
+    mode &= ~FPG_FIM16;         /* unrecoded data */
 
   /* --- prepare data --- */
   fpgrowth = fpg_create(target, supp, 100.0, 100.0, zmin, zmax,
